---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Background Removal"
  description="Fast, Auto, and High quality background removal that keeps your artwork on-device."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <div class="feature-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Background removal
      </nav>

      <div class="feature-kicker"><StatusPill status="available" /></div>
      <h1>Cut out subjects without leaving your document.</h1>
      <p class="feature-intro">
        Varve keeps background removal local and undoable. Choose a simple fast cutout, let Auto
        select a supported installed model, or use High quality when hair, fur, foliage, and thin
        edges deserve more time.
      </p>

      <section class="mode-grid" aria-label="Background removal modes">
        <article class="mode-card site-card site-card--surface">
          <span class="mode-card__number">01</span>
          <h2>Fast</h2>
          <p>Local heuristic masking for flat, studio, and colour-consistent backgrounds.</p>
          <span class="mode-card__meta">No model download</span>
        </article>
        <article class="mode-card mode-card--accent">
          <span class="mode-card__number">02</span>
          <h2>Auto</h2>
          <p>Uses optional IS-Net when installed and keeps bundled U²-NetP available on smaller systems.</p>
          <span class="mode-card__meta">Local · optional 179 MB model</span>
        </article>
        <article class="mode-card site-card site-card--surface">
          <span class="mode-card__number">03</span>
          <h2>High quality</h2>
          <p>BiRefNet Lite for difficult boundaries, with native execution preferred for heavier work.</p>
          <span class="mode-card__meta">Local · optional 224 MB model</span>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Review before you apply</h2>
        <p>
          Review the cutout on a checkerboard before applying it as an editable mask. After Apply,
          use Show Original to compare, or Edit mask to inspect edges against black and white
          backgrounds. Brush refinement, hair-edge refinement, and trimap editing are available
          for further corrections.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Trim to Subject stays bounds-only</h2>
        <p>
          If the goal is a tighter frame rather than a cutout, the crop inspector can detect object
          bounds with an optional local model. Review one or more candidates before applying the
          crop; it never substitutes a detector box for a pixel mask.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section feature-section--note">
        <h2>Honest about difficult pixels</h2>
        <p>
          Models estimate foreground alpha; they do not promise physical matting for glass, smoke,
          steam, or every translucent edge. Unsafe bare-WASM allocations are blocked before they
          can destabilize the editor. AI attempts share a bounded waiting period, and reduced-quality
          fallback is identified in the review. Fast mode needs no model download for simple backgrounds.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Keep fine details under your control</h2>
        <p>
          Optional soft-edge contraction tightens the mask boundary; it does not recolour the
          original pixels. Leave it off for delicate details, then inspect any adjustment before
          keeping it. Source images remain available for further editing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section">
        <h2>Review the edges that matter</h2>
        <p>
          Check hair, thin structures, internal holes, and translucent edges at a useful zoom
          before exporting. A successful run does not guarantee a perfect cutout. Use manual
          mask editing for corrections; optional model downloads require your consent.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="feature-cta">
        <a href={sitePath('/download')} class="btn-default">Download Varve</a>
        <a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/color')} class="btn-secondary">Read the workflow guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .feature-page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0; }
  .breadcrumb { font-size: 0.875rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .feature-kicker { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .feature-page h1 { max-width: 760px; font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem); line-height: 1.02; font-family: var(--font-editorial); color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .feature-intro { max-width: 700px; font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .mode-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .mode-card { min-height: 220px; padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-card); background: var(--surface-card); }
  .mode-card--accent { border-color: var(--border-accent); background: var(--surface-accent-soft); }
  .mode-card__number { color: var(--text-tertiary); font: 0.75rem var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
  .mode-card h2 { margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .mode-card p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
  .mode-card__meta { display: block; margin-top: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .feature-section { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .feature-section h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .feature-section p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; }
  .feature-section--note { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-primary); padding-left: 1rem; }
  .feature-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-default); padding-top: 2rem; }
  .btn-secondary { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--website-radius-control); color: var(--text-primary); text-decoration: none; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .mode-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .mode-card { min-height: auto; } .mode-card h2 { margin-top: 1.5rem; } }
</style>
